    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0625" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756D.5–MAP/2–2851</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-02-28">February 28,
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have today allocated
                    to the Department of Defense the sum of $2,000,000 from funds made available by
                    the Second Supplemental Appropriation Act, 1950<anchor n="1" xml:id="d338-f1"/>
                    to carry out the provisions of section 303(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) of
                    the Mutual Defense Assistance Act of 1949,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d338-f2"/> as
                    amended.</p>
                <p>The allocated funds are to be utilized for programs of military assistance to
                    Indonesia. These programs are to be prepared in general conformity with your
                    letter of February 8, 1951 to the Director of the Bureau of the Budget.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d338-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Truman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d338-f1" n="1" xml:id="d338-f1-content">
                <p>Approved July 26, 1950; 64 Stat. 373.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d338-f2" n="2" xml:id="d338-f2-content">
                <p>Approved October 28, 1949; 63 Stat. 973.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d338-f3" n="3" xml:id="d338-f3-content">
                <p>Frederick J. Lawton. In this letter of February 8, from Secretary of State
                    Acheson to Mr. Lawton, which is not here printed, Mr. Acheson asked that the
                    remaining $2,000,000 of an original $5,000,000 budgeted for equipping the
                    Indonesian constabulary be allocated immediately to the Department of Defense to
                    continue the program (756D.5–MAP/2–851).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
